lib/ - libcgra, the host C library
==================================

The host half of the CGRA. Owns the serial transport, the v2 protocol, the
accelerated kernels, and an in-process emulator that speaks the identical wire
protocol so the whole stack runs with no FPGA.

Layout
------
    include/    public API - cgra.h (the only header you include)
    src/        implementation: transport+kernels, emulator, pty server
    doc/        man page (libcgra.3), hand-written, groff -man

Build (make -f lib.mk <target>)
-------------------------------
    all      build/libcgra.a          (default)
    man      lint + render doc/libcgra.3 -> build/libcgra.3.txt
    clean

Link against it with: cc ... -Iinclude -Llib/build -lcgra

Quick taste
-----------
    cgra_t *d = cgra_open("sim:", 115200);      /* no hardware needed */
    int16_t a[4]={1,2,3,4}, b[4]={10,20,30,40}, out[4];
    cgra_vec_add(d, a, b, out, 4);              /* -> 11 22 33 44 */
    cgra_close(d);

Docs
----
The API is documented in include/cgra.h (Unix-style block comments, no
doxygen) and in doc/libcgra.3. See also the CLI: cgra(1), cgra(5).

Contract
--------
The protocol bytes and config-word layout are shared with hw/rtl/cgra_pkg.vhd.
src/emu.c is the golden reference the RTL testbenches are checked against -
keep header, emulator and VHDL package in lockstep.
